+## HTTPS
+
+To serve the REST API, UI, and gRPC over TLS, set the protocol and provide a certificate and private key. Both files must exist when Flipt starts.
+
+```yaml
+server:
+  protocol: https
+  https_port: 443
+  cert_file: /etc/flipt/tls/cert.pem
+  cert_key: /etc/flipt/tls/key.pem
+```
+
+`http_port` is used when `protocol` is `http`; `https_port` is used when it is `https`. The gRPC listener continues to use `grpc_port` and uses TLS in HTTPS mode. `cors.allowed_origins` accepts either a string or a list of strings.
+
 ## Databases
 
 Flipt supports both [SQLite](https://www.sqlite.org/index.html) and [Postgres](https://www.postgresql.org/) databases as of `v0.5.0`.
